WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.183
Across both the same-stimuli and the novel-stimuli
evaluations,

00:00:04.262 --> 00:00:08.445
the AVFS models predict human similarity judgments
more accurately than baselines trained on semantic labels,

00:00:08.525 --> 00:00:12.707
and they better capture the uncertainty in human
judgments as measured by Spearman correlation.

00:00:12.787 --> 00:00:16.970
Importantly,

00:00:17.050 --> 00:00:21.232
the annotator-specific masks generalize even to
triplets made entirely of novel,

00:00:21.312 --> 00:00:25.495
previously unseen faces,

00:00:25.575 --> 00:00:29.757
which shows the embedding space is far more closely
aligned with the human mental representation

00:00:29.837 --> 00:00:34.020
of faces than spaces learned from rigid categorical
labels.
